    "title": "Is Diego Garcia a U.S. territory?  | Britannica",
    "text": "Ask the Chatbot Games & Quizzes History & Society Science & Tech Biographies Animals & Nature Geography & Travel Arts & Culture ProCon Money Videos Is Diego Garcia a U.S. territory? More Actions Cite Share External Websites Written and fact-checked by The Editors of Encyclopaedia Britannica Encyclopaedia Britannica's editors oversee subject areas in which they have extensive knowledge, whether from years of experience gained by working on that content or via study for an advanced degree.... The Editors of Encyclopaedia Britannica Last updated Mar. 24, 2026 Diego Garcia is not a U.S. territory. The coral atoll, which is located in the central Indian Ocean, is administered by the United Kingdom as part of the British Indian Ocean Territory since 1965, after its separation from Mauritius. In the late 1960s and early 1970s, the island’s civilian population was removed to allow for the development of a military base operated by the United States and the United Kingdom.The legality of the separation has been widely contested, and a treaty to transfer sovereignty from the United Kingdom to Mauritius was signed in May 2025. However, it requires ratification by both countries. As part of the deal, the United Kingdom would have a 99-year lease on the base. Related Questions What is Diego Garcia? What is the sovereignty status of Diego Garcia and what happened to its population? What is the strategic significance of Diego Garcia? Where is Diego Garcia located? Did Iran fire missiles at Diego Garcia in 2026? What is the significance of Diego Garcia? What happened to the Ilois inhabitants of the Chagos Archipelago? What are the recent developments regarding the sovereignty of the Chagos Archipelago? Show More What is Diego Garcia? More Actions Cite Share External Websites Written and fact-checked by The Editors of Encyclopaedia Britannica Encyclopaedia Britannica's editors oversee subject areas in which they have extensive knowledge, whether from years of experience gained by working on that content or via study for an advanced degree.... The Editors of Encyclopaedia Britannica Last updated Mar. 24, 2026 Diego Garcia is a coral atoll, the largest and southernmost member of the Chagos Archipelago, located in the central Indian Ocean. Diego Garcia is strategically significant because of its location and is home to a major military base operated by the United States and the United Kingdom. Developed during the Cold War, the base provides air and naval support facilities that have been used in major military operations. During the 2026 Iran War, Iran—which is about 2,350 miles (3,782 km) away—launched several missiles at the base but none were successful. Related Questions What is the sovereignty status of Diego Garcia and what happened to its population? What is the strategic significance of Diego Garcia? Where is Diego Garcia located? Is Diego Garcia a U.S. territory? Did Iran fire missiles at Diego Garcia in 2026? What is the significance of Diego Garcia? What happened to the Ilois inhabitants of the Chagos Archipelago? What are the recent developments regarding the sovereignty of the Chagos Archipelago? Show More Feedback Corrections? Updates? Omissions? Let us know if you have suggestions to improve this article (requires login). Feedback Type Select a type (Required) Factual Correction Spelling/Grammar Correction Link Correction Additional Information Other Your Feedback Submit Feedback Thank you for your feedback Our editors will review what you’ve submitted and determine whether to revise the article. verifiedCite While every effort has been made to follow citation style rules, there may be some discrepancies. Please refer to the appropriate style manual or other sources if you have any questions. Select Citation Style MLA APA Chicago Manual of Style The Editors of Encyclopaedia Britannica. \" Is Diego Garcia a U.S. territory? \". Encyclopedia Britannica, 24 Mar. 2026, https://www.britannica.com/question/Is-Diego-Garcia-a-